1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:07,540
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:09,760
Thanks, Michelle.

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:19,680
I hope you like it.

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,580
Isn't this baby outfit adorable?

5
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:27,020
With his name on it--"Max."

6
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:29,120
Thanks so much, Harry and Michelle.

7
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,660
We really appreciate it.

8
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:31,740
I'm glad you like it.

9
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:32,620
Michelle picked it out.

10
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,140
Yes, I told Daddy to pick blue ones.

11
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,420
Blue is for boys, and pink is for girls.

12
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,850
And Max is some boy.

13
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:41,580
He's a real Stewart.

14
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:43,580
Right.

15
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,280
That was so thoughtful of you, Michelle.

16
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:49,230
Especially to pick it out in blue.

17
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:52,090
Would you like to see baby Max, Michelle?

18
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:53,890
Could she? Could we?

19
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,060
Could I?

20
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,550
Take them upstairs, Susan.

21
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:58,330
Harry and Michelle can watch Max sleeping.

22
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:02,140
Let's go.

23
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,570
Come on, Michelle.

24
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:06,580
Before Max wakes up.

25
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,380
Will you please take this upstairs, Susan?

26
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:08,880
Uh-huh.

27
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:13,900
Thank you.

28
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:18,300
Michelle is very grown up for a ten-year-old, huh?

29
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:22,090
She's smart and sensitive for her age.

30
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:24,930
Growing up without a mother is difficult.

31
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:28,310
You mature quickly.

32
00:01:28,310 --> 00:01:31,370
Susan's like a mother to Michelle.

33
00:01:31,370 --> 00:01:35,260
They have a good relationship.

34
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:41,200
Do you think Susan and Harry will get married?

35
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:44,610
Yeah. You can count on it.

36
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:47,480
I think so. Yes. They get along so well.

37
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:51,350
I like him. He's good for Susan.

38
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:54,070
He's a little quiet.

39
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:58,250
It's hard to do anything but listen in this family.

40
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,090
You're right, Ellen.

41
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:05,460
Oh, really?

42
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:06,920
It's the way it should be.

43
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,380
The Stewarts are the Stewarts!

44
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,460
They always were,

45
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:10,720
and they always will be.

46
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:11,390
Right!

47
00:02:11,390 --> 00:02:13,450
They've always got an opinion.

48
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:16,520
Always got something to say.

49
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,090
And now there's Max Stewart.

50
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:21,820
and if he talks as loudly as he cries,

51
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:24,320
we're all in for trouble.

52
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,680
He's quiet now.

53
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:39,310
Mmm-hmm. That's because he's sleeping.

54
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:42,100
He's really cute.

55
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:44,190
It's not necessary to whisper, Harry.

56
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:46,040
A baby gets used to voices.

57
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,260
I remember now.

58
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:49,700
We always whispered when Michelle was born.

59
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,550
And I didn't sleep well, Daddy told me.

60
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:52,370
I never slept.

61
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:53,100
And when I did,

62
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,240
I woke up when I heard someone speak.

63
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,080
I bet you were cute.

64
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,200
She sure was.

65
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,800
Not as cute as Max.

66
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:14,540
He's like a little doll.

67
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:15,580
Oh, good.

68
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:19,270
Now I can help diaper him.

69
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:23,540
Let's get Marilyn.

70
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,320
What do you do when he cries like that?

71
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:28,630
You pick him up.

72
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:34,090
He's so little ... so new.

73
00:03:34,090 --> 00:03:38,010
Let's call Marilyn.

74
00:03:38,010 --> 00:04:07,520
Time for a feeding and time for a diapering.

75
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,520
You're a real Stewart.
